1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,150
Seventeen percent of U.S. teens say they
often or sometimes can't finish homework

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,350
because they lack reliable computer or
internet access.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,350
That's Pew Research Center, 2018.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,550
Many of those students work on shared
library computers, public Wi-Fi, or
throttled

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:21,550
phones, where creating an account is a
privacy risk and a dropped signal wipes
the

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:21,950
work.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,916
Maya starts Permission to Learn with no
login.

8
00:00:26,966 --> 00:00:32,502
She misses a two-question pre-check about
a 403 error.

9
00:00:32,552 --> 00:00:41,191
The lesson explains the 403, then she
practises least privilege on a class
roster.

10
00:00:41,241 --> 00:00:48,019
A new two-question post-check asks the
same ideas with different details.

11
00:00:48,069 --> 00:00:56,088
The Before/After Mastery card shows her
growth, and says this is immediate
transfer,

12
00:00:56,138 --> 00:00:57,950
not long-term retention.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,415
She copies an 18-character completion
code.

14
00:01:02,465 --> 00:01:09,857
Leave-no-trace mode stores zero bytes of
progress on the device.

15
00:01:09,907 --> 00:01:17,299
Wipe session, or Escape twice, clears the
tab and confirms.

16
00:01:17,349 --> 00:01:29,206
On her phone, in airplane mode, she enters
the code and the same pack comes back

17
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:29,950
offline.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,764
A language switcher sets Spanish,
including Everyday Fractions, and updates
the page

19
00:01:37,814 --> 00:01:42,973
language so a screen reader can switch
voices.

20
00:01:43,023 --> 00:01:50,787
Our honest testing matrix lists automated
scores, emulated keyboard and zoom checks,

21
00:01:50,837 --> 00:01:57,950
and the manual tests still to do,
including real screen readers.

22
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,050
A teacher writes a short question, watches
the byte count, and prints a QR handout.

23
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:10,910
Scanning the code loads the pack with no
backend.

24
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:19,010
Pasting the student code into Teacher
Verify shows the pack and the pre and post

25
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:19,550
scores.

26
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,870
The checksum catches typos; it is not
forgery-proof.

27
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:24,950
ShareSafe Practice.
